WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.360 --> 00:00:06.290
Lightning strikes above the highest tower
of the imposing, medieval castle standing

00:00:06.290 --> 00:00:08.860
atop the hill in front of you.

00:00:08.860 --> 00:00:14.900
The surrounding landscape beneath the fortress
is a dark forest, just perfect for hiding

00:00:14.900 --> 00:00:17.310
untold numbers of dangers.

00:00:17.310 --> 00:00:23.000
You’re not exactly sure where you are, or
why you were brought here, but you never do.

00:00:23.000 --> 00:00:26.960
It doesn’t matter though, you’ll figure
it all out in due time.

00:00:26.960 --> 00:00:28.550
You always do.

00:00:28.550 --> 00:00:33.920
The context of why you’re brought to the
places you need to be is never important.

00:00:33.920 --> 00:00:38.200
In fact, you don’t pay it any mind at all.

00:00:38.200 --> 00:00:42.690
All that matters is that you help the people
who need it the most.

00:00:42.690 --> 00:00:46.570
Save them from the terror that seems to creep
around every corner.

00:00:46.570 --> 00:00:51.210
No matter where you wind up, it’s always
a struggle.

00:00:51.210 --> 00:00:55.530
These people seem bent on doing everything
in ways that seem to always put them in the

00:00:55.530 --> 00:00:56.930
most danger.

00:00:56.930 --> 00:01:03.070
The world seems to revel in that danger, sometimes
outsmarting you and coming up with new ways

00:01:03.070 --> 00:01:06.880
to hurt and terrify those who you try to help.

00:01:06.880 --> 00:01:08.570
But it doesn’t matter.

00:01:08.570 --> 00:01:09.840
You’re a hero.

00:01:09.840 --> 00:01:16.320
In fact, with how many new places and settings
you seem to instantaneously crop up in, you

00:01:16.320 --> 00:01:18.460
seem to be the hero.

00:01:18.460 --> 00:01:21.030
That’s always how you’ve been.

00:01:21.030 --> 00:01:26.880
You hop from one location to the next, the
days bleeding into one another, never needing

00:01:26.880 --> 00:01:27.880
rest.

00:01:27.880 --> 00:01:31.310
You’re not even sure who you are, in a traditional
sense.

00:01:31.310 --> 00:01:37.450
You don’t know your name, your appearance
is vague and fuzzy, your humanity itself is

00:01:37.450 --> 00:01:41.939
even debatable, but you don’t care about
any of that.

00:01:41.939 --> 00:01:48.950
Deep inside you, there’s a drive, a drive
to help others and save them from the cruelness

00:01:48.950 --> 00:01:52.790
and horrors of the situations they find themselves
in.

00:01:52.790 --> 00:01:57.060
You can never pin it down, but nothing ever
feels right.

00:01:57.060 --> 00:02:01.810
In the places you crop up, things just seem
to work against these folks as much as they

00:02:01.810 --> 00:02:02.810
can.

00:02:02.810 --> 00:02:07.259
Cars don’t start while knife-brandishing
killers pursue them from the woods.

00:02:07.259 --> 00:02:11.009
Undead zombies always seem to know where others
are hiding.

00:02:11.009 --> 00:02:17.060
Ghosts and monsters know the exact ways to
terrify and scare their victims.

00:02:17.060 --> 00:02:24.630
Ordinary, kind people always seem to find
themselves in the most unexplainable, unfortunate

00:02:24.630 --> 00:02:32.410
situations, caught up in tales of the supernatural,
of the arcane, and of absolute terror.

00:02:32.410 --> 00:02:38.220
It’s like the universe is working against
them, putting them in these situations on

00:02:38.220 --> 00:02:39.880
purpose.

00:02:39.880 --> 00:02:42.260
Almost for entertainment purposes.

00:02:42.260 --> 00:02:48.220
But you’re smarter than that, and you have
been for as long as you’ve been doing this,

00:02:48.220 --> 00:02:52.330
which is a very, very long time.

00:02:52.330 --> 00:02:57.170
Jumping from one location to the next, contending
with paranormal activity and supernatural

00:02:57.170 --> 00:03:00.780
foes, saving would-be victims from their clutches.

00:03:00.780 --> 00:03:02.471
You understand that this is your purpose.

00:03:02.471 --> 00:03:08.050
You understand that you are a hero.

00:03:08.050 --> 00:03:09.323
And that’s all you need to know.

00:03:09.323 --> 00:03:13.830
You’ve picked up quite the skillset and
contextual savviness over the thousands of

00:03:13.830 --> 00:03:15.330
times you’ve done this.

00:03:15.330 --> 00:03:20.000
“Don’t go down that alleyway”, “Don’t
split up from a group”, and “Don’t leave

00:03:20.000 --> 00:03:24.959
the house” are some of the more common platitudes
you have to tell the people you meet on your

00:03:24.959 --> 00:03:25.959
journeys.

00:03:25.959 --> 00:03:30.519
They seem obvious enough, but most of the
time, they don’t listen.

00:03:30.519 --> 00:03:35.379
They go on vacation, against your wishes,
and then they find themselves in a haunted

00:03:35.379 --> 00:03:36.610
hotel room.

00:03:36.610 --> 00:03:41.970
They send their kids to a summer camp, only
to find that it’s being stalked by a brutalizing

00:03:41.970 --> 00:03:42.970
slasher.

00:03:42.970 --> 00:03:48.020
They move into a house with a history of being
haunted, and are somehow surprised when the

00:03:48.020 --> 00:03:51.360
spirits don’t take kindly to their new guests.

00:03:51.360 --> 00:03:53.120
To you, it all seems so obvious.

00:03:53.120 --> 00:03:56.790
You’ve seen it all before that it’s predictable.

00:03:56.790 --> 00:04:02.049
But for others, they have a serious difficulty
understanding that their lives are in imminent

00:04:02.049 --> 00:04:03.049
danger.

00:04:03.049 --> 00:04:08.540
For some reason, it’s like they’re predisposed
to doing the exact opposite of what you tell

00:04:08.540 --> 00:04:09.860
them to do.

00:04:09.860 --> 00:04:11.330
But it’s no matter.

00:04:11.330 --> 00:04:16.299
Whatever they wind up doing, you’ll be there
to stop the horrific paranormal threats that

00:04:16.299 --> 00:04:19.229
continuously endanger their lives.

00:04:19.229 --> 00:04:21.999
After all, you’re the hero.

00:04:21.999 --> 00:04:26.390
And so, you set off, moving towards the castle
in the distance.

00:04:26.390 --> 00:04:30.740
You’re not sure of what you’re supposed
to do yet, but you’ll figure it out.

00:04:30.740 --> 00:04:35.430
After a half hour of trekking in the dark,
misty woods, you come across a broken down,

00:04:35.430 --> 00:04:38.860
old school car , stuck in a massive ditch.

00:04:38.860 --> 00:04:42.340
Inside is a young couple, dressed in older
clothing.

00:04:42.340 --> 00:04:47.849
They seem to be elated at your arrival, thanking
you before you’ve even done anything.

00:04:47.849 --> 00:04:52.409
You ask them what happened, and they explain
that while driving, they got lost, and somehow

00:04:52.409 --> 00:04:54.629
found themselves in this forest.

00:04:54.629 --> 00:04:59.509
The fog was so thick, the man explained, that
he lost control of the vehicle entirely, and

00:04:59.509 --> 00:05:01.479
found himself in a ditch.

00:05:01.479 --> 00:05:02.880
You scratch your chin.

00:05:02.880 --> 00:05:05.789
Like most situations you come across, you’ve
seen it before.

00:05:05.789 --> 00:05:10.439
A young couple forced to take refuge in a
dangerous location after their vehicle broke

00:05:10.439 --> 00:05:11.439
down.

00:05:11.439 --> 00:05:16.610
And if you were a betting man, you’d wager
everything you own that the dangerous location

00:05:16.610 --> 00:05:21.580
in question is none other than that creepy
castle on the hilltop.

00:05:21.580 --> 00:05:25.289
You assist the couple, and try to help them
push the car out of the ditch.

00:05:25.289 --> 00:05:28.750
You ask what their plan is, and of course,
they tell you that they’re planning on seeing

00:05:28.750 --> 00:05:31.039
if they can spend the night in the castle.

00:05:31.039 --> 00:05:35.129
You shake your head, wanting to tell them
it’s a bad idea, but if you come out of

00:05:35.129 --> 00:05:37.830
the gate with a warning, it’s going to raise
questions.

00:05:37.830 --> 00:05:41.449
No, your day-saving has to be as natural as
possible.

00:05:41.449 --> 00:05:43.960
At least, when you can help it.

00:05:43.960 --> 00:05:48.559
With some effort, you manage to free the car
from the ditch, setting it on the dirt road

00:05:48.559 --> 00:05:49.559
once more.

00:05:49.559 --> 00:05:53.770
The couple thanks you, but just as they try
to start the car again, a loud spark from

00:05:53.770 --> 00:05:58.150
underneath the hood makes a loud pop in the
silent night air.

00:05:58.150 --> 00:05:59.779
Of course.

00:05:59.779 --> 00:06:04.940
The universe is doing everything it can to
get this helpless couple into that castle.

00:06:04.940 --> 00:06:09.479
After some deliberation, you decide to hold
off on telling them to stay away from the

00:06:09.479 --> 00:06:10.479
castle.

00:06:10.479 --> 00:06:15.370
No reasonable person is going to want to stay
the night in an unfamiliar forest, and given

00:06:15.370 --> 00:06:20.400
the time period you’ve found yourself in,
it’s not like you can call for help.

00:06:20.400 --> 00:06:25.490
Besides, if you stay out here any longer and
delay going into the castle, who knows what

00:06:25.490 --> 00:06:27.490
else the universe will throw at you.

00:06:27.490 --> 00:06:32.099
Maybe you’ll be attacked by wolves, or crushed
under a conveniently falling tree.

00:06:32.099 --> 00:06:37.199
The castle might be their best option for
short-term safety, but it’s almost certainly

00:06:37.199 --> 00:06:40.210
packed with dangers of its own design.

00:06:40.210 --> 00:06:44.389
You tell the couple that you’ll watch their
car, and that you’ll follow them shortly.

00:06:44.389 --> 00:06:47.020
Maybe you can fix it, or figure out what’s
wrong.

00:06:47.020 --> 00:06:50.679
In your travels, you’ve picked up some rudimentary
automobile knowledge.

00:06:50.679 --> 00:06:53.699
Now, it’s time to put it to the test.

00:06:53.699 --> 00:06:59.499
After a cautious goodbye, you watch the two
walk the steep hill to the imposing stone

00:06:59.499 --> 00:07:07.229
castle, and knock on the large, wooden doors
with a timid push of the metal gargoyle door-knocker.

00:07:07.229 --> 00:07:09.809
Now that they’re gone, you can work your
magic.

00:07:09.809 --> 00:07:14.270
You wait until you see the couple greeted
by a woman with black hair and a red dress,

00:07:14.270 --> 00:07:19.590
who welcomes them into the foyer with a concerningly
devilish laugh.

00:07:19.590 --> 00:07:24.179
They’re all so gullible, you think to yourself,
but it doesn’t matter.

00:07:24.179 --> 00:07:26.190
You have a job to do.

00:07:26.190 --> 00:07:28.729
Throughout the night, you scope out the castle.

00:07:28.729 --> 00:07:32.809
Sneaking around the outside, peering in windows
and traversing hidden passageways.

00:07:32.809 --> 00:07:38.249
You’re pretty sure you’re unseen the whole
time, even by the numerous guard dogs and

00:07:38.249 --> 00:07:40.929
strange, giant bat creatures that patrol the
premise.

00:07:40.929 --> 00:07:42.949
Funny how that works.

00:07:42.949 --> 00:07:46.789
When you want to be perceived, you have no
difficulty being noticed, but when you want

00:07:46.789 --> 00:07:49.789
to be hidden, it’s like no one can notice
you.

00:07:49.789 --> 00:07:54.639
While the universe may work against you in
so many ways, it’s also blessed you with

00:07:54.639 --> 00:07:57.759
a variety of benefits and lucky breaks.

00:07:57.759 --> 00:08:03.719
After all, you are the hero of this story,
and of every story you find yourself within.

00:08:03.719 --> 00:08:08.749
You’ve determined, through your impeccably
stealthy sneaking skills, that this castle

00:08:08.749 --> 00:08:14.899
belongs to none other than the Vampire Countess
Lady Brunhild Haas, an immortal creature who

00:08:14.899 --> 00:08:20.699
feasts on the blood of humans and lives out
her days in a creepy, cob-web infested castle.

00:08:20.699 --> 00:08:23.869
A by-the-books vampire, through and through.

00:08:23.869 --> 00:08:27.009
You’ve contended with so many of them at
this point, they’re trivial.

00:08:27.009 --> 00:08:31.469
Heck, you’ve saved hundreds of people from
the infamous Count Dracula, the deadliest

00:08:31.469 --> 00:08:37.750
and most famous vampire of them all, multiple
times across multiple worlds by now.

00:08:37.750 --> 00:08:39.370
You know all the tricks.

00:08:39.370 --> 00:08:44.330
A stake through the heart, a silver bullet,
sunlight, garlic, fire, holy water.

00:08:44.330 --> 00:08:49.611
Now that you think about it, vampire’s are
pretty vulnerable creatures, and if it weren’t

00:08:49.611 --> 00:08:55.110
for their deceptive nature, quick thinking,
magical powers, and hyper-fast reflexes, it’d

00:08:55.110 --> 00:08:57.920
be hard for anyone to find them scary.

00:08:57.920 --> 00:09:04.209
Now understanding your target, it’s time
to play your part as the hero, vanquish this

00:09:04.209 --> 00:09:07.660
monster, and save that couple.

00:09:07.660 --> 00:09:11.370
Just as the Countess is planning to sneak
into the guest bedroom, where the couple is

00:09:11.370 --> 00:09:15.730
sleeping, and sink her fangs into their necks,
you leap from the shadows with a wooden stake

00:09:15.730 --> 00:09:20.290
you found inside the castle’s catacombs,
and hit her in the head with as much force

00:09:20.290 --> 00:09:21.290
as possible.

00:09:21.290 --> 00:09:24.899
It’s not enough, and the Countess lunges
forward, screeching.

00:09:24.899 --> 00:09:29.630
The couple jolts awake, just in time to witness
the Countess and you duking it out in the

00:09:29.630 --> 00:09:30.940
guest bedroom.

00:09:30.940 --> 00:09:36.360
Seeing a vulnerable spot, the countess transforms
into a bat and flies toward the girl to attack,

00:09:36.360 --> 00:09:41.839
but the Countess got greedy, because unfortunately
for her, she couldn’t predict that she was

00:09:41.839 --> 00:09:44.960
within throwing distance of the stake you
picked up.

00:09:44.960 --> 00:09:49.800
You hurl it forward, precision striking the
transformed countess right in the wing.

00:09:49.800 --> 00:09:54.470
Injured, she changes back into her human form,
giving you enough time to pull the stake from

00:09:54.470 --> 00:09:59.769
what was her wing and is now her bloody arm,
and drive it straight through her heart and

00:09:59.769 --> 00:10:02.250
seal her fate forever.

00:10:02.250 --> 00:10:07.100
It's not pretty, and you’re now covered
in vampire blood, but you got the job done.

00:10:07.100 --> 00:10:10.360
The couple is shocked, but they both saw it
with their own eyes.

00:10:10.360 --> 00:10:16.100
The countess was a vampire, she transformed
into a bat, and they need to get out of there.

00:10:16.100 --> 00:10:20.500
You guide them through the castle, narrowly
avoiding the locations of all the guarding

00:10:20.500 --> 00:10:24.970
creatures, and into a room containing the
countess’s horse-drawn carriage.

00:10:24.970 --> 00:10:30.089
You set them off on their way just as the
sun rises, and remind them to not forget the

00:10:30.089 --> 00:10:33.490
luggage in the back of their car that’s
still in the woods.

00:10:33.490 --> 00:10:37.899
You feel a sense of satisfaction, as you always
do after your quests.

00:10:37.899 --> 00:10:43.079
But as soon as that feeling washes over you,
you’re whisked away to a different location.

00:10:43.079 --> 00:10:45.680
But this time, something is different.

00:10:45.680 --> 00:10:49.500
You blink, and you wind up in what appears
to be a facility.

00:10:49.500 --> 00:10:53.860
You’ve been to some place similar before,
but nothing like this.

00:10:53.860 --> 00:10:58.759
It’s massive, filled with dozens upon dozens
of people rushing from hallway to hallway.

00:10:58.759 --> 00:11:03.959
And in those hallways are doors, oh, so many
doors.

00:11:03.959 --> 00:11:09.759
You scratch your head, but the confusion disappears
as you grab a young man in an orange jumpsuit

00:11:09.759 --> 00:11:14.630
by the shoulders and inform him that he’s
about to be terminated due to misconduct in

00:11:14.630 --> 00:11:15.649
a research environment.

00:11:15.649 --> 00:11:21.189
You’re not even sure what that means, but
the words come out of you like they’re preordained.

00:11:21.189 --> 00:11:25.139
It felt like the right thing to say, and you’re
not exactly wrong.

00:11:25.139 --> 00:11:30.959
The man pushes your hand away, swearing at
you before moving forward, presumably to his

00:11:30.959 --> 00:11:31.959
death.

00:11:31.959 --> 00:11:35.839
Four armed guards approach you from the distance,
and before you know it, you’re taken to

00:11:35.839 --> 00:11:41.680
a room with a two way glass, a microphone,
and a strange device strapped around your

00:11:41.680 --> 00:11:47.110
neck, called by one of the labcoats as a “Scranton
Reality Anchor”, whatever that means.

00:11:47.110 --> 00:11:51.730
They’ve given you a name.

00:11:51.730 --> 00:11:52.730
SCP-2786.

00:11:52.730 --> 00:11:56.519
And from what you can glean, they know quite
a bit about you.

00:11:56.519 --> 00:12:01.290
A suited individual sits down across the two-way
glass and begins asking you questions.

00:12:01.290 --> 00:12:04.930
You don’t have time for this, you have business
elsewhere.

00:12:04.930 --> 00:12:09.939
You explain to the Agent, as he calls himself,
that you’re a hero, who goes from place

00:12:09.939 --> 00:12:12.910
to place, wherever you’re called upon.

00:12:12.910 --> 00:12:18.269
Those in distress, those suffering, you’re
their champion.

00:12:18.269 --> 00:12:23.769
The agent asks why they found you inside horror
movies and books, and you’re taken back.

00:12:23.769 --> 00:12:24.769
Books?

00:12:24.769 --> 00:12:25.769
Movies?

00:12:25.769 --> 00:12:26.959
What is he talking about?

00:12:26.959 --> 00:12:31.920
You explain that your work is very real, and
that before the incident with the vampire,

00:12:31.920 --> 00:12:37.660
you just finished dispatching of a hockey-mask
wearing slasher at Camp Crystal Lake and saving

00:12:37.660 --> 00:12:39.320
a group of teenagers.

00:12:39.320 --> 00:12:41.260
It was easy work for you, of course.

00:12:41.260 --> 00:12:46.259
He was just one guy, and those kids ignored
all of the obvious warning signs.

00:12:46.259 --> 00:12:51.209
The agent confirms that he saw you do that,
and you’re even more confused.

00:12:51.209 --> 00:12:52.630
He was there?

00:12:52.630 --> 00:12:57.800
The agent catches himself, and explains that
while he wasn’t exactly there, he watched

00:12:57.800 --> 00:12:59.990
it play out in the movie.

00:12:59.990 --> 00:13:05.410
He tries to explain that all of your adventures
are taking place in fictional locations.

00:13:05.410 --> 00:13:07.629
Movies, books.

00:13:07.629 --> 00:13:14.250
You, SCP-2786, enter these mediums through
mysterious, unknown means, and alter their

00:13:14.250 --> 00:13:16.270
plots entirely.

00:13:16.270 --> 00:13:21.089
Copies of films and books that you enter are
changed, and the characters always manage

00:13:21.089 --> 00:13:25.470
to escape the horror of the film due to your
assistance.

00:13:25.470 --> 00:13:29.629
You alter stories early, change them entirely.

00:13:29.629 --> 00:13:30.680
Movies?

00:13:30.680 --> 00:13:31.720
Books?

00:13:31.720 --> 00:13:35.600
This is not only ridiculous, but it’s also
getting on your nerves.

00:13:35.600 --> 00:13:39.470
The agent is wasting your time, and you have
to go save those guys in the orange jumpsuits

00:13:39.470 --> 00:13:42.819
from being terminated or reassigned, or whatever
it is!

00:13:42.819 --> 00:13:48.600
You stand up, and the anchor device somehow
turns itself off and detaches from your neck.

00:13:48.600 --> 00:13:53.339
You phase through the wall on your left, unsure
exactly of how you did it, but it felt natural.

00:13:53.339 --> 00:13:55.970
Maybe that’s how this world works.

00:13:55.970 --> 00:14:00.220
Certain people can do things like this, and
these guys are trying to contain them.

00:14:00.220 --> 00:14:03.680
Like a government organization, or the Men
in Black.

00:14:03.680 --> 00:14:06.709
Your genre-savviness pays off yet again.

00:14:06.709 --> 00:14:12.579
Whatever this SCP Foundation is, you’ve
read them like an open book, and now that

00:14:12.579 --> 00:14:17.240
you understand the situation, you can do what
you were sent here to do.

00:14:17.240 --> 00:14:21.339
You hear the sound of an alarm in the distance,
but you can’t be stopped.

00:14:21.339 --> 00:14:25.850
Over the next few hours, you break into multiple
containment cells, freeing orange jumpsuits,

00:14:25.850 --> 00:14:31.589
or D-Class Personnel, as they’re called
by the Foundation, as well as several other

00:14:31.589 --> 00:14:37.399
kind, regular people who just happen to have
anomalous abilities contained within the site.

00:14:37.399 --> 00:14:39.950
These Foundation types disgust you.

00:14:39.950 --> 00:14:44.529
Thinking they can lock up human lives without
regard for their rights or dignity, studying

00:14:44.529 --> 00:14:45.529
them.

00:14:45.529 --> 00:14:49.070
You bet that they want to study you too, but
they’re not going to.

00:14:49.070 --> 00:14:54.120
As soon as you feel your work is done, you’re
whisked away to another location, away from

00:14:54.120 --> 00:14:59.850
the strange Foundation facility and into an
ordinary American city, where you assist a

00:14:59.850 --> 00:15:05.889
cast of characters in narrowly avoiding the
traps and sinister games of a killer puppet

00:15:05.889 --> 00:15:08.069
who wants to murder them.

00:15:08.069 --> 00:15:12.339
But after getting the job done this time,
you’re not taken anywhere new.

00:15:12.339 --> 00:15:16.250
You’re in the same location, over and over
again.

00:15:16.250 --> 00:15:17.509
On a loop.

00:15:17.509 --> 00:15:22.100
After the 48th time saving these characters,
you start to consider what the agent had told

00:15:22.100 --> 00:15:23.100
you.

00:15:23.100 --> 00:15:26.700
You enter films, books, horror stories.

00:15:26.700 --> 00:15:28.389
You’re… fictional.

00:15:28.389 --> 00:15:30.079
Well, meta-fictional.

00:15:30.079 --> 00:15:32.930
You exist inside the work and out of it.

00:15:32.930 --> 00:15:38.220
The prospects of this are strange and new,
but if they’re true, it might explain why

00:15:38.220 --> 00:15:41.519
you’ve never felt like the people you save.

00:15:41.519 --> 00:15:47.790
Like you always felt like you were in a story,
that you were the only ‘real’ person there.

00:15:47.790 --> 00:15:52.050
If everyone else is just a character, what
does that make you?

00:15:52.050 --> 00:15:53.050
Alone?

00:15:53.050 --> 00:15:54.060
Entirely?

00:15:54.060 --> 00:15:58.790
If you’re inside a movie right now, can
someone be looping it, playing back the DVD

00:15:58.790 --> 00:16:02.180
over and over again to keep you trapped there?

00:16:02.180 --> 00:16:03.440
Is it the Foundation?

00:16:03.440 --> 00:16:06.430
Is this how the Foundation is going to contain
you?

00:16:06.430 --> 00:16:08.209
No, you tell yourself.

00:16:08.209 --> 00:16:11.320
You are not going to be contained.

00:16:11.320 --> 00:16:13.850
Another 30 loops of the same, monotonous ordeal.

00:16:13.850 --> 00:16:17.199
But then, you’re transported somewhere new.

00:16:17.199 --> 00:16:21.360
You laugh to yourself, having somehow escaped
the trap planted by the Foundation.

00:16:21.360 --> 00:16:26.040
Before you know it, you’ll be off to a new
story, and you can continue doing what you

00:16:26.040 --> 00:16:27.040
do best.

00:16:27.040 --> 00:16:31.660
But as the world fades out around you, it
doesn’t seem to come back.

00:16:31.660 --> 00:16:36.279
You seem to be stuck in a sea of white, and
black, and red.

00:16:36.279 --> 00:16:40.910
Those same colors, over and over, extending
on forever.

00:16:40.910 --> 00:16:46.850
You walk for what seems to be hours, and as
you do, surroundings begin to form around

00:16:46.850 --> 00:16:47.850
you.

00:16:47.850 --> 00:16:48.850
A concrete wall.

00:16:48.850 --> 00:16:50.410
A concrete floor.

00:16:50.410 --> 00:16:51.490
A bed.

00:16:51.490 --> 00:16:56.430
A door, leading to another endless sea of
white, red, and black.

00:16:56.430 --> 00:16:58.740
And on the floor, a logo.

00:16:58.740 --> 00:17:02.999
A circle within a circle, with three arrows
pointing inwards.

00:17:02.999 --> 00:17:08.530
For the first time in your life, you’re
unsure of what you should be doing.

00:17:08.530 --> 00:17:15.669
That logo, it’s the logo of the SCP Foundation,
and you look like you’re inside a containment

00:17:15.669 --> 00:17:16.669
cell.

00:17:16.669 --> 00:17:17.669
No.

00:17:17.669 --> 00:17:22.059
You pound against the wall, collapsing it
and allowing the sea of white swallow you

00:17:22.059 --> 00:17:23.059
whole.

00:17:23.059 --> 00:17:24.059
More logos.

00:17:24.059 --> 00:17:25.059
More empty brackets.

00:17:25.059 --> 00:17:26.059
A file.

00:17:26.059 --> 00:17:28.419
You’re inside a file.

00:17:28.419 --> 00:17:30.950
No, a cell of your own design.

00:17:30.950 --> 00:17:34.169
You’re creating the containment cell.

00:17:34.169 --> 00:17:38.929
Your own brain, however it works, is generating
a narrative.

00:17:38.929 --> 00:17:44.000
The narrative of you being contained by the
SCP Foundation.

00:17:44.000 --> 00:17:49.860
A horror story, and that’s exactly what
the Foundation used to trap you.

00:17:49.860 --> 00:17:55.740
You’re not sure where you are, nor can you
feel your body or even your sense of self.

00:17:55.740 --> 00:17:58.740
All that you know is that you’re trapped.

00:17:58.740 --> 00:18:04.530
You’ve been whisked away to a new story
alright, your story, and it seems to be harder

00:18:04.530 --> 00:18:06.700
and harder to escape from.

00:18:06.700 --> 00:18:12.020
But then, the cell around you collapsed once
more, and you found yourself in a familiar

00:18:12.020 --> 00:18:13.020
setting.

00:18:13.020 --> 00:18:16.250
A medieval castle, being urged by a queen
to slay a great evil.

00:18:16.250 --> 00:18:17.250
You managed to escape!

00:18:17.250 --> 00:18:23.250
You don’t know how you did it, but you’re
back to your old life, jumping from story

00:18:23.250 --> 00:18:24.280
to story.

00:18:24.280 --> 00:18:28.590
You know all the beats, all the cliches, and
all of the right things to do.

00:18:28.590 --> 00:18:34.010
And for the next few hours, you do them, slaying
the great beast and stealing his divine amulet

00:18:34.010 --> 00:18:35.970
to bring back to the kingdom.

00:18:35.970 --> 00:18:38.169
But after the fact, it felt hollow.

00:18:38.169 --> 00:18:39.809
It didn’t feel real.

00:18:39.809 --> 00:18:41.669
Not like the other times.

00:18:41.669 --> 00:18:47.049
You weren’t sure how a location could tell
a lie, but this one felt as if its truth were

00:18:47.049 --> 00:18:48.049
paper-thin.

00:18:48.049 --> 00:18:52.380
Was someone pulling the strings and making
this world a lie for them?

00:18:52.380 --> 00:18:54.820
Like trickery, or an illusion.

00:18:54.820 --> 00:18:59.880
And suddenly, just as you begin to suspect
this narrative to be another means of containment

00:18:59.880 --> 00:19:05.620
generated by the Foundation, everything goes
back to that white containment cell.

00:19:05.620 --> 00:19:07.640
They can’t keep you here.

00:19:07.640 --> 00:19:10.690
They can’t keep you here.

00:19:10.690 --> 00:19:13.940
You repeat it over and over, shouting it into
the distance.

00:19:13.940 --> 00:19:16.020
You just want to go home, you beg.

00:19:16.020 --> 00:19:17.850
They can’t control you.

00:19:17.850 --> 00:19:20.950
You’re the hero of this story.

00:19:20.950 --> 00:19:24.230
If you’re fictional, you’re a good character!

00:19:24.230 --> 00:19:26.950
You did everything right!

00:19:26.950 --> 00:19:32.590
You don’t understand, this is YOUR story,
and it will always be your story.

00:19:32.590 --> 00:19:36.390
The Foundation is just another one of the
countless villains you’ve fought.

00:19:36.390 --> 00:19:40.640
Those self-rightous murderers, you will surpass
them!

00:19:40.640 --> 00:19:46.130
You shout into the void of television static
and endless torment for what seems like decades.

00:19:46.130 --> 00:19:50.940
And when you tire of your yelling, you realize
one thing.

00:19:50.940 --> 00:19:52.590
This is eternal.

00:19:52.590 --> 00:20:00.070
Now go check out “SCP-1230 - A Hero Is Born”
and “SCP-423 - Self-Inserting Character”

00:20:00.070 --> 00:20:04.160
for more plot-twisters and story-hoppers from
SCP Explained!

